#519 sgirandomcolour -- PRE-TABLE CHECK, written 2026-09-10 ~04:2x BEFORE table 1 runs (mtime is the proof).
Instrument: regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py -- 5 witness rows (agy, 2/5 on HEAD 1ce8296, 5/5 on the
fix) + 9 detector rows appended by the main loop.  Diff under review: src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c
(scratchpad/patch_sgirc.py, 58 changed lines): SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12 as the last enumerator, an `ok'
local in the PUT branch, the default arm declining (ok = 0, once-latched announce keeping the old
`[ put: color mode = 0x%x ]' literal as its prefix), the store guarded by `if (ok)'.  Product code
otherwise untouched; the GET default arm is NOT in scope (sgirebufuninit).

1. SIBLING PARITY
   The PUT default arm's sibling is the GET default arm in the same function (reads raw, announces
   per pixel, unlatched) -- NOT touched here; its row is sgirebufuninit and it is DISCLOSED in the
   contract.  The TLB/mode switch's default (SGIRE_W_BADMODE, #504) is the nearest de-fatalised
   sibling: latched, returns before any store.  Channels there: announce once, `*color' untouched.
   Channels here: announce once (its OWN bit -- `latch indep' rows the independence), destination
   untouched (`ycrcb put', `reserved put', `two declined', `indep paint').  ASYMMETRY: #504's arm
   RETURNS; this one falls through to the common tail with the store skipped -- deliberate (the
   sketch rule: the tail's memory_rw is the only thing after the switch, and it is what the guard
   skips), and the `two declined' row is what pins "skipped" rather than "returned early" for the
   second PUT.
2. CLAIM -> ROW
   "the STORE IS SKIPPED, so the destination keeps what the guest had"     -> ycrcb put, reserved put,
                                                                              two declined, indep paint
   "not a zero fill"                                                        -> ycrcb put (0 would red)
   "announce is latched on its own bit"                                     -> once, latch indep
   "the old literal is kept as the prefix: the witness attributes on it"   -> ycrcb attrib (unchanged),
                                                                              announce text
   "A declined PUT never reads buf"                                          -> no row: not observable
                                                                              (no store); SENTENCE.
   "Twelve of the sixteen type nibbles reach here"                          -> two driven (0xf0, 0x50);
                                                                              the arm does not read the
                                                                              value; SENTENCE (contract).
   "main.c seeds random() per process"                                      -> the witness's determinism
                                                                              row measured it; no fix row.
3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
   Guard: color_mode (a local from `mode').  Body: `ok', d->warned.  The shared field d->warned now
   has thirteen bits; the disagreeing state the rule asks for is another site's bit set first --
   built in-session by `latch indep' (SGIRE_W_BADMODE fired by a LIN_B PUT, then the colour decline).
   `ok' is a local written only by the default arm: its disagreeing state is "second declined PUT in
   the same process with the latch already set", built by `two declined'.
4. CHANNEL -- per row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs
   ycrcb put / reserved put   (b) reinstatement (random fills + store); M_noguard (`if (ok)' removed:
                              stores an unassigned buf); M_zerofill (buf = 0, ok = 1)     -> word != paint
   two declined               M_okinlatch (`ok = 0' moved inside the latch condition)      -> word != paint
   once                       M_nolatch (latch guard removed)                              -> count 2
   latch indep                M_sharedbit (SGIRE_W_BADMODE used instead of BADCOLOR)       -> count 0
   indep paint                M_sharedbit does not vary this; (b) does (LIN_B returns; YCRCB stores) -> word
   announce text              (b) (old text only) ; M_silent (announce removed)             -> count 0
   live silent                M_declineall (ok = 0 for every type) ; M_announceall            -> count 1 / word
   ci8 / rgb / abgr put       M_dropcase_X (the case removed -> falls to default -> paint)  -> word
   VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION CHECK: `indep paint' is fixed under M_sharedbit (both PUTs skip their
   store either way) -- it is a CONTROL for `latch indep', named as such; every other row's channel
   varies under its named mutant.
5. THE (d) ENUMERATION FOR TABLE 1 (bounded to the diff's hunks):
   dominating predicates: `put' (unchanged), `switch (color_mode)' (each supported type its own
   case; the default is one cell), `if (ok)' (introduced), the latch test (introduced).  Cells:
   {default declines / stores} x {latch kept / removed / shared} x {store guard kept / removed /
   inside-latch} x {supported types kept / one dropped}.  Planned mutants, one edit each:
   M1_reinstate (b)   M2_noguard   M3_zerofill   M4_okinlatch   M5_nolatch   M6_sharedbit
   M7_silent          M8_declineall   M9_dropcase_ci   M10_dropcase_abgr   M11_null (the pre-fix
   file wholesale)    M12_announce_prefix_dropped (the old literal removed from the text: kills
   `ycrcb attrib' -- an L4-shaped mutant; recorded because the prefix is load-bearing for the witness)
   ACCEPT rows: live (RGBA), ci8 put, rgb put, abgr put; growth mutants M9/M10 (a case dropped) and
   M8 (everything declined).

6. PASS-2 CORRECTIONS TO SECTIONS 1-5 (APPENDED 2026-09-10 ~04:3x, AFTER table 1 had started at 04:06 and
   after the pass-2 panel `_scratchpad/panel_20260910_040019/'; sections 1-5 above are as written at 03:51,
   unedited -- the corrections are appended so the order stays legible).
   a. Section 4 mis-assigned M_declineall to `live silent' (codex).  `ok = 0' for every type declines the
      RGBA accept PUT, so the word stays the PAINT and the row that reds is `live' (want FG_VAL); the
      announce sits in the default arm only, so `live silent' keeps its 0 under M_declineall.  `live
      silent' is killed by M_announceall ONLY (announce in every arm -> count 1).  M8_declineall's kill
      is therefore owed to `live', not to `live silent' -- read table 1's M8 reds against that.
   b. The diff description in the header ("58 changed lines") is the NON-BLANK count.  Measured against
      scratchpad/dev_sgi_re.pre519.c: 3 hunks, 48 additions (3 of them blank) and 13 deletions =
      61 changed lines (`diff | grep -cE '^[<>]''); the earlier figure came from `^\+[^+]', which cannot
      match an added blank line (codex).
   c. Section 4's `two declined' -> M_okinlatch is kept, but the CONTRACT's claim that the row pins
      "skipped rather than returned early" is withdrawn (grok Q4.4, minimax): after the PUT switch the
      guarded store is the ONLY statement, so `if (ok)' and an early `return' are observationally
      identical.  The row pins that the second declined PUT does not store; nothing pins the guard's form.
   d. Section 1's asymmetry sentence ("`two declined' is what pins skipped rather than returned early")
      is withdrawn for the same reason; the asymmetry between #504's `return' and this arm's fall-through
      is REAL and is a readability choice, not an observable.
   e. `indep paint' (section 4) observes ONLY the YCRCB half: setup_put() re-paints the destination before
      the second PUT, so whether the LIN_B PUT stored is overwritten before the load (grok Q4.3).  Its note
      is reworded in the instrument; it remains the named CONTROL for `latch indep'.
   f. TWO ONE-TOKEN ESCAPES of the 14-row instrument, both found by grok from the packet, one confirmed by
      codex, neither in section 5's enumeration:
        - `if (ok)' -> `if (ok || x)': every PUT sat at vertex (0,0).  A cell the (d) enumeration missed:
          the guard qualified on a value the body READS (x, y are body-read lvalues; the body's own test
          of them is the bounds check `x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= 2048 || y >= 2048' for the tiled path and
          `x >> 12 >= 32' for the linear one, so {origin, non-origin} is a body-induced partition).  ROW
          OWED and added: `ycrcb x4y1' + `x4y1 announce' (vertex (4,1); the LINEAR path computes
          `ofs = x & 4095', a BYTE offset with y ignored, so x=4 reaches the second pre-painted word, and
          y=1 makes the `|| y' form store too).  Mutants M13_okorx, M14_okory in table 2.
        - SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR -> SGIRE_W_TEX_RD (or any of the ten other bits BADMODE excepted): the
          independence row fires BADMODE only.  DISCLOSED under clause (e): the body tests exactly one bit
          and never TEX_RD, so the other-bit cells are values the body never distinguishes; rowing one
          session per bit is the unbounded shape the CHANNEL rule refuses.  Built anyway as M15_texrd so
          the disclosure carries a measured score.  The own-bit convention is enforced by the enum's own
          comments (#498 measured a shared bit at 23/25) and by reading.
   g. The first cut of the (4,1) row was (1,0) with the comment "ofs = 1 * bufdepth = 4" -- WRONG for the
      linear path (byte 1, straddling words 0 and 1; a store there would still have changed word 1's low
      byte, so the row would have reddened by accident rather than by construction).  Corrected before any
      table ran on it (this file, the instrument's block comment).  The fourteen pre-existing sessions'
      command streams are byte-unchanged by the repair (the second-word paint is emitted only for a
      non-origin vertex; diff against sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.FROZEN.py shows only the header sentence,
      setup_put's vertex branch, the contract comment, the new block and the `indep paint' note text), so
      table 1's per-row kills carry over; table 2 measures BASE and the three new mutants only.
   h. THREE MORE DISPOSALS (appended ~04:5x, before table 2 copied its baseline; table 1 is still running on
      its own frozen pair and is untouched):
        - PRODUCT, one token: the announce closed its bracket twice -- `[ put: color mode = 0x%x ] sgi_re:
          ... (once) ]' (grok "cosmetic", minimax item 5).  Now `[ put: color mode = 0x%x ] [ sgi_re: ...
          (once) ]', two bracketed units mirroring the BADMODE sibling's `[ sgi_re: unimplemented dst_mode
          ... (once) ]'.  No row or mutant reads the bracket: ANN keys on `unimplemented colour type in
